ason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915068710,"responseId":"msg_011Ce787fGXYtqqws8cCmeee","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01U8ghFjZaG5wah6ziJ5zAae","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_name\",\"state_abbr\",\"farmers_markets\",\"csa_programs\",\"farm_stands\",\"snap_ebt_markets\",\"snap_ebt_pct\",\"organic_vendor_markets\",\"organic_pct\",\"markets_with_website\",\"website_pct\"\n\"California\",\"CA\",647,95,223,100,15.5,114,17.6,246,38.0\n\"New York\",\"NY\",555,156,272,41,7.4,45,8.1,283,51.0\n\"Pennsylvania\",\"PA\",426,102,886,18,4.2,43,10.1,226,53.1\n\"Minnesota\",\"MN\",390,62,80,101,25.9,14,3.6,148,37.9\n\"Illinois\",\"IL\",370,64,713,29,7.8,42,11.4,155,41.9\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915074627},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01QstLW3j7fukx1GaprWgfsU","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"NAME\",\"POPESTIMATE2025\"\n\"United States\",341784857\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915074627},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I have:\n- U.S. population in 2025: 341,784,857\n- Now I need to sum the farmers_markets column to get the total number of farmers markets\n\nLet me get the total farmers markets count.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01TAGKNnUtrEmFhvmjRgEci3","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.aggregate(total_markets=source.farmers_markets.sum())"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":174,"cacheRead":19139,"cacheWrite":709,"totalTokens":20036,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0008700000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0019139,"cacheWrite":0.00088625,"total":0.00368415},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":58},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915074628,"responseId":"msg_011Ce788624EhJTQYpnLPsCR","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01TAGKNnUtrEmFhvmjRgEci3","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"total_markets\"\n7944\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915078042},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! So I have:\n- Total farmers markets: 7,944\n- U.S. population: 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to calculate the ratio: 7,944 / 341,784,857 * 100,000\n\nLet me create a build script that joins these two pieces of data and computes the metric. Following the skill's pattern for cross-dataset metrics, I need to:\n1. Read both sources\n2. Get the total farmers markets count from farmers_markets table\n3. Get the US population from census_population table\n4. Join them with a constant key\n5. Calculate the ratio\n\nLet me create the build script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I need to create a metric that calculates farmers markets per 100,000 residents. I'll build a script that joins both datasets and computes the ratio."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01HWRyCtaAYiyoAZYc17FriH","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data and sum the total\nfarmers = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so)\n\n# Read census data and filter for US total\npopulation = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets to a single total\nmarkets_total = (farmers\n    .aggregate(total_markets=farmers.farmers_markets.sum())\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Get US population from census data\nus_pop = (population\n    .filter(population.NAME == \"United States\")\n    .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join on the constant key and calculate the ratio per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    markets_total.join(us_pop, markets_total.k == us_pop.k)\n    .mutate(markets_per_100k=markets_total.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":743,"cacheRead":19848,"cacheWrite":222,"totalTokens":20825,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0037150000000000004,"cacheRead":0.0019848,"cacheWrite":0.0002775,"total":0.0059893},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":152},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915078042,"responseId":"msg_011Ce788KpmgVwBZ9ZBH9Wgy","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01HWRyCtaAYiyoAZYc17FriH","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1320 bytes to .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915085429},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me build this script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01GUf4NNPqhUh9djScrKM4K2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-62-cwshtg_a && xorq build .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/bp_metric.txt && cat /tmp/bp_metric.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":140,"cacheRead":20070,"cacheWrite":785,"totalTokens":21008,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0007000000000000001,"cacheRead":0.002007,"cacheWrite":0.00098